IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nfp-dates`
IMPORT `nfp-rules`
IMPORT `nfp-seat`

-- Family Provision Act 1970 (NT) -- worked cases for the family member's questions (nfp-seat.l4), the date helper
-- (nfp-dates.l4) and the s 9 regulative rule (nfp-rules.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited
-- text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not
-- about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- UNOFFICIAL. Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is owned by the Northern Territory. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`any day` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000

-- s 7 with the s 7(7) heads: relationship, then order, maintaining, contributing, more than nominal, a court could order,
-- then the grandchild's three facts, then the parent's two.
GIVEN r IS A `Relationship to the deceased`, o IS A BOOLEAN, m IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, n IS A BOOLEAN, k IS A BOOLEAN, pd IS A BOOLEAN, pa IS A BOOLEAN, pm IS A BOOLEAN, s IS A BOOLEAN, ch IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`entitled` r o m c n k pd pa pm s ch MEANS `Am I entitled to apply` r o m c n k pd pa pm s ch

`spouse` MEANS `spouse or de facto partner at the death`
`former` MEANS `former spouse or former de facto partner`
`child` MEANS `child, including one born alive after the death`
`other` MEANS `another relationship, or none`

§§ `s 7 -- who may apply`

-- A spouse or de facto partner, and a child, with nothing else: entitled (s 7(1)(a), (c)).
#ASSERT `entitled` `spouse` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `entitled` `child` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A former spouse not maintained: not entitled (s 7(2)); with a maintenance order in force at the death: entitled (s 7(7)(a)).
#ASSERT `entitled` `former` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `entitled` `former` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A stepchild: a nominal contribution is not maintenance; a more than nominal one is; maintaining is; a court's power to order is (s 7(7)(b), (c)).
#ASSERT `entitled` `stepchild` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `entitled` `stepchild` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `entitled` `stepchild` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `entitled` `stepchild` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A "more than nominal" answer without any contribution counts for nothing.
#ASSERT `entitled` `stepchild` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A grandchild whose parent (the deceased's child) died first: entitled (s 7(3)(a)).
#ASSERT `entitled` `grandchild` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A grandchild with a living parent who was not maintaining them: entitled (s 7(3)(b)).
#ASSERT `entitled` `grandchild` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A grandchild with a living parent who was maintaining them: not entitled, even though the deceased maintained them too (finding 2).
#ASSERT `entitled` `grandchild` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A parent maintained by the deceased, though the deceased left a spouse: entitled (s 7(4)(a)).
#ASSERT `entitled` `parent` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A parent not maintained: entitled only if the deceased left no spouse or partner and no child (s 7(4)(b)).
#ASSERT `entitled` `parent` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `entitled` `parent` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `entitled` `parent` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Anyone else (a sibling, a carer, a friend): the Act does not list them (NOTHING, fork F2), however maintained.
#ASSERT `entitled` `other` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `entitled` `other` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 7(7) alone: no head holds.
#ASSERT `s 7(7) -- I was maintained by the deceased immediately before the death` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `s 9 -- by what day, and whether in time`

#ASSERT `By what day must I apply` TRUE (`d` 15 3 2025) EQUALS `the last day to apply is` (`d` 15 3 2026)
#ASSERT `By what day must I apply` TRUE (`d` 31 12 2025) EQUALS `the last day to apply is` (`d` 31 12 2026)
-- A grant on 29 February: the last day is 28 February (fork F1).
#ASSERT `By what day must I apply` TRUE (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `the last day to apply is` (`d` 28 2 2025)
#ASSERT `By what day must I apply` FALSE (`d` 15 3 2025) EQUALS `the 12 months have not begun: no administration has been granted in the Territory`

-- grant, filing, extended, extended to, estate fully distributed
GIVEN g IS A DATE, f IS A DATE, x IS A BOOLEAN, xd IS A DATE, fd IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Timing`
`timing` g f x xd fd MEANS `Is my application in time` TRUE g f x xd fd

`grant` MEANS `d` 15 3 2025

-- The last day, and the day after.
#ASSERT `timing` `grant` (`d` 15 3 2026) FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS `in time (s 9(1))`
#ASSERT `timing` `grant` (`d` 16 3 2026) FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS `out of time, but I may apply to the Court to extend the time (s 9(2), (3))`
-- Filed on the day of the grant, and the day before it.
#ASSERT `timing` `grant` `grant` FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS `in time (s 9(1))`
#ASSERT `timing` `grant` (`d` 14 3 2025) FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS `no administration has been granted in the Territory yet, so the 12 months have not begun (s 9(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` FALSE `grant` (`d` 1 6 2025) FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS `no administration has been granted in the Territory yet, so the 12 months have not begun (s 9(1))`
-- Late, and the estate already lawfully and fully distributed: no extension can be sought (s 9(4)).
#ASSERT `timing` `grant` (`d` 16 3 2026) FALSE `any day` TRUE EQUALS `out of time, and an extension can no longer be sought: the estate has been lawfully and fully distributed (s 9(4))`
-- In time, with the estate distributed: still in time (s 9(4) touches only an extension).
#ASSERT `timing` `grant` (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE `any day` TRUE EQUALS `in time (s 9(1))`
-- Extended to 30 June 2026: in time on 16 March and on 30 June, late on 1 July.
#ASSERT `timing` `grant` (`d` 16 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 30 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS `in time, within the time the Court extended (s 9(2))`
#ASSERT `timing` `grant` (`d` 30 6 2026) TRUE (`d` 30 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS `in time, within the time the Court extended (s 9(2))`
#ASSERT `timing` `grant` (`d` 1 7 2026) TRUE (`d` 30 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS `out of time, but I may apply to the Court to extend the time (s 9(2), (3))`
-- A 29 February grant: 28 February 2025 in time, 1 March late.
#ASSERT `timing` (`d` 29 2 2024) (`d` 28 2 2025) FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS `in time (s 9(1))`
#ASSERT `timing` (`d` 29 2 2024) (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS `out of time, but I may apply to the Court to extend the time (s 9(2), (3))`

-- The regulative rule directly: 365 days allowed (15 March 2025 to 15 March 2026); filing at day 365 and day 366.
#ASSERT `filing at` 365 `satisfies` (`the application must be filed within` 365)
#ASSERT (NOT (`filing at` 366 `satisfies` (`the application must be filed within` 365)))
-- Late, the trace leaves the applicant's permission to seek an extension (the LEST), not FULFILLED.
#TRACE `the application must be filed within` 365 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 366)

§§ `s 10 -- serving the administrator`

#ASSERT `Must I serve notice of my application on the administrator` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I serve notice of my application on the administrator` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I serve notice of my application on the administrator` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 7, 8, 9 -- can the Court order provision`

-- relationship, maintained, parent died first, a parent alive, a living parent maintaining, left spouse, left child, in time, satisfied, conduct
#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me` `spouse` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Court may order such provision as it thinks fit, in its discretion (s 8(1))`
#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me` `spouse` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Court may refuse an order because of your character or conduct (s 8(3))`
#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me` `spouse` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no order: the Court is not satisfied that adequate provision is not available (s 8(1))`
#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me` `spouse` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `out of time, and the time has not been extended (s 9)`
#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me` `former` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not entitled to apply (s 7)`
#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me` `former` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Court may order such provision as it thinks fit, in its discretion (s 8(1))`
#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me` `grandchild` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Court may order such provision as it thinks fit, in its discretion (s 8(1))`
#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me` `parent` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not entitled to apply (s 7)`
#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me` `other` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not list you among those who may apply (s 7(1))`

§§ `s 13 -- property appointed by will`

#ASSERT `Can provision for me come out of property appointed by the will` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Can provision for me come out of property appointed by the will` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`Can provision for me come out of property appointed by the will` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Can provision for me come out of property appointed by the will` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Can provision for me come out of property appointed by the will` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Can provision for me come out of property appointed by the will` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE))

§§ `ss 20, 21 -- property already distributed`

-- Grant 15 March 2025; filed on the last day (15 March 2026) and the day after.
#ASSERT `Can provision come out of property already distributed` `grant` (`d` 15 3 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Court may order provision out of the distributed property (s 20(1))`
#ASSERT `Can provision come out of property already distributed` `grant` (`d` 16 3 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `section 20 gives no power here: my application was not made within 12 months after the grant`
#ASSERT `Can provision come out of property already distributed` `grant` (`d` 15 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `section 20 does not speak to a distribution made after the administrator had notice of my application`
#ASSERT `Can provision come out of property already distributed` `grant` (`d` 1 6 2025) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: the order would disturb a proper distribution for a dependant of the deceased (s 20(2))`
-- An application filed before the grant is not "made within 12 months after" it.
#ASSERT (NOT (`the application was made within 12 months after the grant` `grant` (`d` 14 3 2025)))

#ASSERT `Can I sue the administrator for distributing` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: section 21 bars that action against the administrator`
#ASSERT `Can I sue the administrator for distributing` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: section 21 bars that action against the administrator`
#ASSERT `Can I sue the administrator for distributing` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `section 21 does not bar it: whether the action lies is for the general law`
#ASSERT `Can I sue the administrator for distributing` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `section 21 does not bar it: whether the action lies is for the general law`

§§ `ss 16, 17, 19, 14 -- once an order is made`

#ASSERT `How does the order for me take effect` `a will disposes of the whole estate` EQUALS `as a codicil to the will, made immediately before the death (s 16(1))`
#ASSERT `How does the order for me take effect` `there is no will` EQUALS `as a change to the intestacy rules for that property (s 16(2))`
#ASSERT `How does the order for me take effect` `a will disposes of only part of the estate` EQUALS `as a codicil for the property the will disposes of, and a change to the intestacy rules for the rest (s 16(1), (2))`

#ASSERT `Can the Court change the order made for me` `someone else` `discharge, reduce or suspend the order` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `section 17 gives no power on this application: it is not made by the administrator or a person interested in the estate`
#ASSERT `Can the Court change the order made for me` `the administrator` `increase the provision` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: section 17(3) bars an order under section 17(1) increasing the provision`
#ASSERT `Can the Court change the order made for me` `a person beneficially entitled to or interested in part of the estate` `discharge, reduce or suspend the order` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Court may discharge, vary or suspend the order (s 17(1))`
#ASSERT `Can the Court change the order made for me` `the administrator` `discharge, reduce or suspend the order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Court may discharge, vary or suspend the order (s 17(1))`
#ASSERT `Can the Court change the order made for me` `the administrator` `discharge, reduce or suspend the order` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Court may discharge, vary or suspend the order, or make such other order as is just (s 17(2))`
-- An increase sought where s 17(2) applies: not barred by s 17(3) in its words (finding 5, fork F7).
#ASSERT `Can the Court change the order made for me` `a person beneficially entitled to or interested in part of the estate` `increase the provision` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Court may discharge, vary or suspend the order, or make such other order as is just (s 17(2))`

#ASSERT `Will a mortgage or assignment of my provision have effect` TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`Will a mortgage or assignment of my provision have effect` FALSE))

#ASSERT `What must I give back if the presumed dead person is alive` FALSE TRUE 20000 50000 EQUALS `nothing under section 14`
#ASSERT `What must I give back if the presumed dead person is alive` TRUE FALSE 20000 50000 EQUALS `nothing under section 14`
#ASSERT `What must I give back if the presumed dead person is alive` TRUE TRUE 0 50000 EQUALS `restore the property, or at my option pay its value when I received it, of` 50000
#ASSERT `What must I give back if the presumed dead person is alive` TRUE TRUE 20000 0 EQUALS `pay back the money I received, of` 20000
#ASSERT `What must I give back if the presumed dead person is alive` TRUE TRUE 20000 50000 EQUALS `restore the property or pay its value, and pay back the money, totalling at most` 70000
#ASSERT `What must I give back if the presumed dead person is alive` TRUE TRUE 0 0 EQUALS `nothing under section 14`
